    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_857979dbdf6a0c1b366df6317fc9ebfe188a1e77833aa2960357c9ea69e12486",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Changing the target value in zeta(s)=a and evolving the completed function through the de Bruijn-Newman heat family are different perturbations with different stability structures. Nonzero a-point fibers need not preserve critical-line alignment, whereas heat-flow real-rootedness is monotone in time and is therefore summarized by a single boundary Lambda, making valid cross-time implication possible.",
