    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_9d52c822ffc76ed689040c75e808b79d2a651ec327a41d36a88d9ef3f4b326ee",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Across these routes, an attractive representation-level fact does not supply the stronger interior condition that would do the proof work: zeta partial sums approximate zeta but have forbidden right-half-plane zeros, the proposed de Branges space fails the required positivity, and local-factor ratios have unit boundary modulus yet are unbounded and hence not inner. The reusable comparison is to factor a strategy into its visible representation and its stronger sign, zero-free, or norm antecedent, then test that antecedent independently.",
