    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_ac4e2b180aeef43d6fa6ae5b7e5ff5bddf1b5bb961d2cd27fc9ecb680d10bb46",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The analytic route to the prime number theorem requires exclusion of zeta zeros on Re(s)=1 and a Tauberian transfer from logarithmic-derivative boundary behavior to prime asymptotics. The explicit formula shows why RH is stronger: a zero rho=beta+i gamma contributes at x^beta scale, so the sharper error term demands beta=1/2 rather than merely beta<1.",
