    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_ca73ce9d2eb2303cf845a368bdae097e4f6949740aa45d29f505a9cd00c7eac1",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "A visually or numerically exceptional local event is only a search candidate. Lehmer's near-cancellation discussion motivates targeted stress-region searches, while the later close-pair work makes a pair relevant to Lambda only after converting ordinates to H_0 coordinates, coupling the gap to all other zeros through g_k(0), and composing one-sided local, distant-block, and tail bounds to verify the Lehmer threshold.",
