      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Exact RH criteria can preserve truth while exposing mutually different observables: Farey discrepancy norms, cyclotomic growth, function-space density, infinitely many coefficient signs, determinant growth, and divisor inequalities. Shared equivalence to RH supplies no bridge among these observables and no evidence that the translated universal estimate is easier.",
