    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_dfcf6c2956a4c15782eb646c9fd2429da983cd2d0f4e7c6dc5f01f8fa98134e1",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The finite-field comparison identifies a sign-producing structure, not merely a carrier: an algebraic index theorem forces negative semidefiniteness in the geometric analogue. By contrast, the higher-genus correspondence program constructs a carrier while leaving differential action and a generalized norm unresolved, and the semi-local operator program constructs canonical local traces while treating globally compatible principal-value normalization and positivity as conjectural burdens.",
